[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m $ ./translation/target/release/driver 7 1000000 3 | head -c 1 >/dev/null
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # ${PIPESTATUS[0]} == 0     (WRONG)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Cause: Rust-runtime-imposed signal state that has no counterpart in the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m program. Fix: `restore_default_sigpipe()` in `translation/src/main.rs` calls
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)` as the first statement of `main`, via a direct
