[38;5;252m[1m## What I found[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The translation was already highly faithful — it correctly preserves every C quirk I could find (the [38;5;10m& 25[0m trace-alphabet bug, [38;5;10mprocess_a_stream[0m's always-[38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m clamp from the [38;5;10msize_t[0m vs [38;5;10mlong long[0m promotion, case 9's duplicated pop loop, the three distinct functions named [38;5;10mtarget[0m, the persistent [38;5;10mstate_a[0m/[38;5;10mflipflop[0m statics, [38;5;10mstrtol("")[0m accepting an empty argv entry as [38;5;10m0[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mOne real mismatch, in exit status:[22m Rust's runtime installs [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m. Writing to a closed stdout returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, which every [38;5;10mlet _ = write!(...)[0m discarded, so the Rust program exited [38;5;10m0[0m where the C program was killed by the signal (141).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10m./c_src/build/driver 7 1000000 3 | head -c 1   ->  C 141,  Rust 0
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fixed with [38;5;10mrestore_default_sigpipe()[0m in [38;5;10mtranslation/src/main.rs[0m — a direct [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m call to [38;5;10msignal(SIGPIPE, SIG_DFL)[0m, no new dependency. This is invisible to any test that only checks stdout on short programs; it needs a trace long enough to fill a pipe buffer.[0m[0m
